+| #401 | 2026-08-18 | **PART C — AND-7 FULL BLEED: the Android system-bar strip stops existing (Damir's top ask, #396).** #391 made the strip MATCH each screen; he wants the screen to REACH the top — *"full bleed to the top"*, named for the WALLET HERO and the launch gradient. Root cause was already at source (`docs/android-findings.md:47`): the window draws edge-to-edge and both bars are transparent, but `MainActivity`'s insets listener then padded the ROOT CONTENT VIEW down by `sysInsets.Top`, so every page — WebView included — started below the status bar and the visible strip was the root background. **That top padding is gone.** The inset now travels to the shells as a `*SL{AndroidInsetTop}` carrier in CSS px (physical px ÷ `DisplayMetrics.Density`), set into `--android-inset-top` by a head-top script in **all 18 shells** before first paint, and consumed through ONE new expression in `base.css`: `--safe-top: max(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px), var(--android-inset-top, 0px))`. Android's `env(safe-area-inset-top)` cannot carry it — it reports the display CUTOUT only, which is exactly why the iOS-#282 chrome measured 0 here. **Every top safe-area site in the tree now reads `--safe-top`** (topbar · wallet hero · launch · lock · call bar · call overlay · media viewer · chat select), pinned STRUCTURALLY: a raw `env(safe-area-inset-top)` anywhere outside `base.css` fails the run, because such a site is silently 0 on the one platform this fixes. **Deliberately NOT changed: the BOTTOM.** The root still pads it, because that padding carries the IME inset and the Android keyboard behaviour was measured on exactly that mechanism (#334/AND-16); a bottom variable would either double-pad the bottom nav or re-open the keyboard round, and neither is what "full bleed to the top" asked for. **Three ordering traps found and closed while building.** ① The FIRST document is generated before the insets listener has ever fired — `MauiApplication.OnCreate` builds the MAUI app, whose `App` ctor sets `MainPage`, whose page ctor runs `loadPage → generatePage` — so `MainApplication.OnCreate` registers a BOOTSTRAP estimate from the platform's `status_bar_height` dimension before `base.OnCreate()`, and the listener replaces it with the authoritative value. Without it the very first screen paints its topbar under the clock. ② An unknown `*SL{}` key is not silently empty — `localizeHtml:207` LOGS an error for it on every page load, and `ixian.log` is a file the user shares with the engineer — so the key is SEEDED to "0" in `SpixiLocalization`, which is also the correct value on iOS/MacCatalyst/Windows. ③ The Android-15 modal branch padded every modal by `MainActivity.Insets.Value.Top / 3` — a hardcoded density divide that existed only because the root padding did not reach a modal container. It is REMOVED: with no root top padding every page is unpadded the same way, and the lock, call and scan shells pad themselves like the rest. **Two pages must NOT be asked to handle the inset and keep native padding:** the 8 remaining legacy `Raw/html` pages (`hasLegacyPageChrome`) and **mini-app pages**, whose content is third-party and cannot be assumed inset-aware — `!hasGeneratedContent` is true exactly there, because `MiniAppPage` never calls `loadPage`. ★ The same one-token classification was added to the **iOS** branch, which is the fix `security-review-for-be-engineer.md` **MAJOR #6(b)** asks for: mini-app UIs have rendered under the notch and the home indicator since #282. MAJOR #6(a), the link-handoff trust tier, stays open. ★ **The measurement ships instead of blocking** (#294/#304, and the unattended answer from #398): the dev HUD now prints `INSET var=… env=… safe=…` beside the C# counters, so if a full-bleed screen looks wrong the line says which of the three numbers is at fault rather than starting a guessing round. It also carries the **F-5 boot timeline** (`rdy` / `flush` / `done` / `zero`, ms from document start) — see #399. Dev-mode gated, no storage, no bridge verb. | Matching a strip is a workaround for not being able to paint under it. Once the WebView owns the whole window the colour question disappears on every screen at once — and the #391 strip colours stay as the pre-paint frame, which is what they should have been all along | ✅ built · 🟡 F5 + the probe numbers |
